# Stage G4 field gate: does the tilted deviatoric eigenstrain actually leave a
# shear stress at the dislocation glide planes after relaxation?
#
# The Stage G diagnosis showed that under p p f a laterally uniform eigenstrained
# slab relaxes sigma_zz to ~0 by simply getting taller. The same equilibrium
# argument (d sigma_xz/dz = 0 with a traction-free top) can null the SHEAR
# component too, leaving only the ridge shape differential. This gate measures
# Delta sigma_xz between physical and control BEFORE spending 16 GPU-hours.
# Minimization only, no dynamics: ~5 min per case.
# Variables (-var): DATA_FILE, POT_DIR, OUT_PREFIX

units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p f

read_data       ${DATA_FILE}

pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * ${POT_DIR}/Jelinek_2012_meamf AlS SiS MgS CuS FeS ${POT_DIR}/Jelinek_2012_meam.alsimgcufe AlS FeS MgS SiS

neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check no

compute         st all stress/atom NULL virial

region          bottom block INF INF INF INF INF 6.0 units box
group           bottom region bottom
fix             hold bottom setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0

thermo          100
thermo_style    custom step atoms temp pe press pxz
min_style       cg
min_modify      dmax 0.1
minimize        1.0e-8 1.0e-10 3000 30000

write_dump      all custom ${OUT_PREFIX}.gate.lammpstrj id type x y z c_st[1] c_st[2] c_st[3] c_st[4] c_st[5] c_st[6] modify sort id
